From 8761e921cf910b6a48dadbaea23e3ed379c185ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:15:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Characters: Wind Waker HD's light on the Mirror Shield, the
 sword's grip, ice, Chus, bombs and chests

The HD actor light took only the main toon pattern (ramp mix, times the albedo texel, then nothing or the effect
light): 1,328 of the disc's 1,812 toon materials. Three more patterns now take it, right after the albedo stage, with
the stages after it run on the lit colour as the GameCube ran them:
- E, the colour-register albedo: stage 1 is C1 x the ramp mix, its texture an environment map read for its alpha
  (the Mirror Shield's face, the Master Sword's grip, ice arrows and blocks, Chus, Stalfos). The albedo is C1,
  linearised as the texel is, and there is no rim (Wind Waker HD's "rim-only" materials). The sheen stage
  (K x the map's alpha, or K x a texel) is added after the light.
- F, a register added to stage 1 (C1, C2 or K: the bomb's flash before it goes off): added after the light and
  clamped as the stage clamps.
- G, the main pattern then other stages (the chests' decal mixed by A1, threshold compares, sheens, Ganondorf's
  ramp-alpha highlights): run unchanged on the lit colour.
After stage 1 every stage must write PREV and read it. A later stage in the effect light's form (PREV + K x the
ramp) is left out of HD's result, as the main pattern's is. 1,567 of 1,812 (86.5%) now match; of the materials
Wind Waker HD lights as toon, 1,498 of 1,625 (92.2%, was 79.4%). DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_HD_EXT=0 keeps only the main
pattern, to compare.

gxcore tests: the main pattern's WGSL is byte for byte what it was (3,096 keys, 32 of them matched before); the new
patterns' modules compile with Dawn. On Linux at Outset's pier at noon only the Mirror Shield's face changes (from
white to lit grey with its crest showing); Link, his hair and the shield's rim are the same.

Characters: no rim on Wind Waker HD's light for the added-register pattern (the bomb, the Tingle statues)

The added-register pattern (F: stage 1 adds C1, C2 or a konst colour after the albedo, the bomb's flash before it
goes off) kept HD's rim, on the guess that only the bomb among its materials was rim-only in HD. Wind Waker HD's
material table says all 28 of the disc's F materials are rim-only (edge 1 with no edge colour, intensity or
sharpness, the edge term compiled out): Link/bomb/Bom1, the Tingle statues Vtil* and Vtin*, Os, Oq, VbakH, Ktaru,
Rd, Pw and the rest. So F now takes no rim, as E, from TEV state alone; the main pattern and G keep theirs.

gxcore tests: the bomb's key (and F with C2 or a konst colour) matches with no rim, its WGSL has no rim term.

Characters: the GameCube's effect light on Wind Waker HD's light, until HD's light buffer is ported

HD's character light dropped the GameCube's effect-light stage (PREV + K1 x the ramp), on the grounds that HD's
toon shader has no such term and sends the effect lights to its light buffer instead. That buffer isn't ported, so
under the HD look Link and the islanders lost the sword-hit flash, the bombs' flash and the item-get light.

The stage is the GameCube's effect light alone: settingTevStruct_eflightcol_plus sets K1 from the effect light
that reaches the model, and setLightTevColorType_sub cuts the material's stage count back to before the stage
whenever K1 is unset. With no effect the draw has two stages and nothing is added, so restoring it brings back
nothing HD lacks on a daylit character. The stage now runs on HD's colour as the GameCube ran it on its own:
HD's light right after the albedo stage (as for E, F and G), then PREV + K1 x the ramp, clamped. The same goes
for E, F and G's effect stages, which were skipped. DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_HD_EFFECT=0 (HdActorLightConstants
screen.z 0) leaves the stage out, as before, to compare.

gxcore tests: the main pattern with the stage has HD's block after stage 1 and the stage after it, kept or left
out by screen.z; without it the block is after the last stage as before. The changed modules compile with Dawn.

Characters: the Mirror Shield's glint added in linear light on Wind Waker HD's light, as HD adds it

The GameCube's SHMSBMAT ends in PREV + K3.r x APREV (K3.r 96, APREV the glint texture's alpha plus the ice
ramp's): an add, which RecompCore ran as GX after HD's light, on the gamma colour. Wind Waker HD's face shader
(PS 2960, in an HD capture) adds the same term in linear light before the clip: U2 x L + U7.x x
clamp(ramp.a + I4), with U2 = C1 linearised and U7.x = 0.1166 = (96 / 255)^2.2. So a streak on a shaded face
came out about 60 levels too bright (208, 231, 254 against HD's 146, 161, 180); in full sun both clip white.

toon_light_stage() marks pattern E's later PREV + KONST x APREV stage (sheen_stage). HD's block then adds the
konst colour linearised times stage 1's alpha to its light before the clip, and the GX stage's own add is taken
back out after it (its alpha still runs). The same TEV is on the shield, every Master Sword grip, the ice
arrow's tip, the icerock parts, bottles and the rest of the 42 GameCube materials with that tail; only the
shield has an HD trace. The Chus' K x texel sheen and the other patterns' stages are unchanged.

gxcore tests: the shield's key matches with sheen_stage 2, its WGSL adds hd_sheen in the light and restores
HD's colour after stage 2; the Chus and the main pattern with the same stage keep it a GX stage. The shield's
module compiles with Dawn (Vulkan, core and compatibility).
